\f3\fs26 For the dark man the 216 floor trip to street level seemed to take forever. He was in the starting blocks and was sprinting even before the doors were fully open, a particle pulse pistol was now in his hand as he charged out to the street, but there was no-one there. Not the meat wagon and not the blank. 
\f4\i Economy be damned!
\f3\i0  The blank was supposed to be waiting. He really wished that just one of these jobs wasn\'92t a cluster fuck, but they always were. Always. He wasn\'92t looking forward to filing this report, the Director was not going to be happy.\
* * *\
\'93Let me get this straight, Agent Jones.\'94 said the incredulous Director of Pre-Emptive Reciprocity and Pro-active Euthanasia. (P.R.P.E.) \'93The blank lost the Gyges disc and you lost the blank. Does that about sum it up?\'94\
\'93I wouldn\'92t chose to describe it in those terms\'94 replied the soon to be demoted field operative. \'93The blank was really unwell. He could barely stand, but insisted on being juiced up with AMT to complete the contract. He made it look like suicide, but he somehow dropped the disc. I went up to retrieve it, but the office had been sanitized and a new tenant had moved in.\'94\
\'93You idiot. You could be identified.\'94\
\'93No, I had my disc. Security records would have been scrambled.\'94\
\'93I mean by people in the building. Did you speak to anyone?\'94 The director could not believe a fully trained agent could be this obtuse.\
\'93No\'85..No I didn\'92t.\'94 He figured he had better start lying. This truth telling bullshit was getting him nowhere. He decided to keep the cleaner out of it, at least until he knew what this street sweeper had pinched from Mr. Lee\'92s office.\
\'93What happened with the blank?\'94 The Director inquired.\
\'93He had finished the job, there was a company meat-wagon around the corner and I was about to pop him off, when we discovered the cloak (disc) was missing. I went to fetch it and when I got back he was gone and so was the van.\'94\
\'93So you lost the blank, a cloak and a van. A good days work and it\'92s not even midday.\'94 The director stared him down. \'93This was a baby-sitting job, Agent Jones. He kills them, you kill him. Easy. You had better find that blank and silence him.\'94\
\'93And the disc?\'94\
\'93Find that too. We can\'92t have just anyone waltzing through secure zones at will. Violating the privacy of citizens is our job.\'94\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94 Agent Jones said, very glad this conversation was over.
